## Ownership

- Shared and durable: edit `~/src/boilerplate/home/...`, apply, and reconcile.
- Machine-local or OS-owned: change the live setting on the target host.
- Home router, firewall, DHCP, or DNS appliance state: use `opnsense`.
- Inspect where a value lives before deciding ownership.

Common shared state includes shells, agent harnesses, terminals, Omarchy desktop
overrides, and shipped user services. Input speed, display scaling, battery
policy, Bluetooth pairing, and app login state are normally machine-local.

For Omarchy/Linux work, read [references/omarchy.md](references/omarchy.md).
For macOS work, read [references/macos.md](references/macos.md).

## Completion

Re-read each changed setting or file. For shared changes, verify rendered live
output after a targeted apply. Report any required logout, reconnect, reload,
or restart.
